[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/issues/9","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/issues/9/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/issues/9/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/issues/9/events","html_url":"https://github.com/0xPolygon/x402-rs/pull/9","id":4795469875,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQTfa0c7tLN93","number":9,"title":"chore: stop advertising unsupported `upto` scheme on Polygon facilitator","user":{"login":"AkshatGada","id":96907514,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcaw-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96907514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada","html_url":"https://github.com/AkshatGada","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-02T14:38:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T13:46:45Z","closed_at":"2026-07-06T13:46:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/pulls/9","html_url":"https://github.com/0xPolygon/x402-rs/pull/9","diff_url":"https://github.com/0xPolygon/x402-rs/pull/9.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/0xPolygon/x402-rs/pull/9.patch","merged_at":"2026-07-06T13:46:45Z"},"body":"## What\n\nStop advertising the **`upto`** scheme (`v2-eip155-upto`) on the Polygon facilitator. It is removed from `config_from_env()` so it no longer appears in `/supported` (and `/health`), and `verify`/`settle` for an upto payload return a graceful `unsupported_scheme`. **The upto implementation is left fully compiled in** — this only stops registering the scheme.\n\n## Why\n\nLive testing against the deployed Amoy facilitator showed `upto` is broken on the multi-instance deployment:\n\n- The `upto` scheme binds each payment to **one specific facilitator signer** (the Permit2 witness `facilitator` field; the on-chain proxy enforces `msg.sender == witness.facilitator`).\n- The deployment runs **≥3 instances behind a load balancer, each with a disjoint signer set**. `supported()` advertises a random signer from the responding instance, but verify/settle are round-robined to other instances → `500 \"Missing signing credential for 0x…\"` (~2/3 of attempts). In some cases funds moved on-chain while the client received a 402 (settle/response desync).\n- `upto` is **Permit2-only by design** (EIP-3009 can't express \"up to\" amounts), so there is no fallback rail.\n\nThe proper fix (shared signer set across instances, or signer-aware routing) is an infrastructure effort. Until then, advertising `upto` misleads consumers into attempting a flow that mostly fails. `exact` (v1/v2, both EIP-3009 and Permit2 rails) is unaffected and verified working (16 live Amoy settles).\n\n## Changes\n\n- `facilitator/src/config.rs` — remove the `v2-eip155-upto` `SchemeConfig` from `config_from_env()` (with an explanatory comment); update the `config_from_env` unit test to assert upto is absent (schemes len 3→2).\n- `facilitator/config.json.example` — drop the `v2-eip155-upto` entry so a copied config doesn't re-enable it.\n- **Not changed:** the `V2Eip155Upto` blueprint wiring (`run.rs`), the builder impl (`schemes.rs`), and the entire `crates/chains/x402-chain-eip155/src/v2_eip155_upto/**` implementation — all retained, just unused, so re-enabling is a one-line change once infra supports it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test -p x402-facilitator --features full config` — passes (2/2).\n- Booted locally (env-driven, `CHAIN_ID=80002`): `/supported` and `/health` list only `exact` (v2 `eip155:80002` + v1 `polygon-amoy`), **no `upto`**.\n- upto payload → `POST /verify` and `POST /settle` return `unsupported_scheme` (HTTP 400), no crash.\n- The deployed facilitator uses the env-var config path (no config.json is copied in the Dockerfile), so this change covers production once the new image is deployed.\n\n## Follow-up (not in this PR)\n\n- Infra fix to actually support `upto` (shared signer set or signer-aware routing), then re-register the scheme.\n- Optional: skip the `v2-eip155-upto-*` conformance tests (they spawn a single-instance facilitator where upto still works, so they're unaffected by this change).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","closed_by":{"login":"adamdossa","id":2633913,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MzM5MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2633913?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa","html_url":"https://github.com/adamdossa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/issues/9/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/issues/9/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/issues/8","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/issues/8/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/issues/8/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/issues/8/events","html_url":"https://github.com/0xPolygon/x402-rs/pull/8","id":4766952970,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQTfa0c7rt6Ql","number":8,"title":"Sync to upstream v2.0.1 — activate Permit2 on Polygon","user":{"login":"AkshatGada","id":96907514,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcaw-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96907514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada","html_url":"https://github.com/AkshatGada","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AkshatGada/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-06-29T09:45:46Z","updated_at":"2026-06-30T09:56:31Z","closed_at":"2026-06-30T09:56:31Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/0xPolygon/x402-rs/pulls/8","html_url":"https://github.com/0xPolygon/x402-rs/pull/8","diff_url":"https://github.com/0xPolygon/x402-rs/pull/8.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/0xPolygon/x402-rs/pull/8.patch","merged_at":"2026-06-30T09:56:31Z"},"body":"## What\n\nSync this fork to **upstream x402-rs v2.0.1** (134 upstream commits) while preserving the Polygon-specific commits, plus one follow-up fix required by an upstream API change.\n\n- Merge `upstream/main` (v1.3.0-era → **v2.0.1**) into the fork.\n- Preserve Polygon commits: env-driven facilitator config (`config_from_env`), structured JSON logging, and the `0xpolygon/x402-facilitator` CI image.\n- Fix: `RpcConfig.http` became `LiteralOrEnv<Url>` upstream — adapt `config_from_env()` (`facilitator/src/config.rs`).\n\n## Why\n\nProduction (`main`) cannot settle Permit2 payments on Polygon: it hard-codes Permit2 proxy addresses that were **never deployed on-chain**, and lacks the EIP-2612 `settleWithPermit` (gasless-approval) path. v2.0.1 brings:\n- the **correct, on-chain-deployed** proxy addresses (`0x402085c248…0001` exact, `0x4020A4f3b7…0002` upto — both verified live on Polygon mainnet **and** Amoy), and\n- the EIP-2612 `settleWithPermit` path.\n\nThis is required for the wallet team's **x402 smart-session signer**, which relies on Permit2.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun against this branch with `--features full`:\n\n- **Unit tests:** 129 passed, 0 failed (workspace excluding the pre-existing TRON failure — see below).\n- **Release binary:** `cargo build -p x402-facilitator --features full --release --locked` ✅\n- **Docker image:** builds (`x402-facilitator:v2.0.1`).\n- **Container boot (env-driven, mainnet 137):** `/health` → 200; `/supported` lists `exact` + `upto` on `eip155:137`; logs confirm the env-config fallback and structured JSON logging.\n- **Live end-to-end Permit2 settles on Polygon mainnet (the definitive proof):** client signed a Permit2 authorization → facilitator verified → settled on-chain via the deployed exact Permit2 proxy `0x402085c248EeA27D92E8b30b2C58ed07f9E20001` (status success in both cases). Two independent tokens:\n  - **USDC** (supports EIP-3009): tx `0x0d7b57ab899e9d10a697f45a5345b84a7a439a08963c01cc7d7fcd2a0ffa2937`; moved 0.01 USDC, allowance consumed by exactly the payment.\n  - **USDT0** (does **not** support EIP-3009 — so Permit2 is the only rail): tx `0xbb81a39a96d2c381eb5b5bca7c61c402d8cf394a28b3a79056d731ac2b5325ad`; moved 0.01 USDT, allowance consumed by exactly the payment. This conclusively exercises the Permit2 path for an arbitrary ERC-20.\n\n## Known issue\n\n- One pre-existing **upstream** unit-test failure: `x402-chain-tron::networks::tests::permit2_proxies`. It fails identically on pristine `upstream/main` (not introduced by this sync), and TRON is unused by this deployment.\n\n## Caveats\n\n- The sync also pulls upstream TRON / Aptos / Solana changes (full v2.0.1). A partial cherry-pick was rejected because it would re-introduce the proxy-address / Permit2-witness mismatch.\n- Bundled-approval for undeployed wallets is **EIP-2612-specific** (`settleWithPermit`) — works for USDC and other 2612 tokens.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","closed_by":{"login":"adamdossa","id":2633913,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MzM5MTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2633913?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa","html_url":"https://github.com/adamdossa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamdossa/gists{